@startuml
left to right direction

actor Student
actor Administrator

rectangle "Smart Campus Study Room Booking System" {

    usecase "View Availability" as UC1
    usecase "Book Room" as UC2
    usecase "Cancel Booking" as UC3
    usecase "Block Room" as UC4
    usecase "Unblock Room" as UC5
    usecase "Review Usage" as UC6
    usecase "Display Confirmation" as UC7
}

Student --> UC1
Student --> UC2
Student --> UC3

Administrator --> UC4
Administrator --> UC5
Administrator --> UC6

'why: R4 - Successful booking produces an immediate confirmation
UC2 ..> UC7 : <<include>>

'why: US-03 - Confirmation displayed upon successful cancellation
UC3 ..> UC7 : <<include>>

note right of UC1
Assumption:
The library system displays the
current status of all rooms
in real time.
end note

note right of UC2
Booking Rules (R1-R3):
- Start time in future
- Duration 1 to 2 hours (R2)
- Room unblocked (R3)
- No overlapping bookings
end note

note right of UC3
Assumption:
A student can only cancel
a booking that they
previously created.
end note

note right of UC4
Assumption:
Blocking a room prevents
new bookings for that room.
end note

note right of UC5
Assumption:
Unblocking restores
availability for future
time slots.
end note

note right of UC6
Assumption:
System logs record completed
and cancelled bookings.
end note

note right of UC7
Assumption:
Confirmation details are
displayed immediately
in the web application.
end note

@enduml